1
00:00:00,209 --> 00:00:01,524
One hundred push-ups.

2
00:00:01,791 --> 00:00:02,502
Every day.

3
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:03,864
For thirty days.

4
00:00:04,132 --> 00:00:06,073
That's three thousand push-ups.

5
00:00:06,363 --> 00:00:08,116
You can't even do twenty.

6
00:00:08,407 --> 00:00:09,370
Exactly.

7
00:00:09,352 --> 00:00:10,546
So I tested it.

8
00:00:10,813 --> 00:00:12,249
Twenty-two on day one.

9
00:00:12,516 --> 00:00:14,271
Thirty-eight on day thirty.

10
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,721
But the push-ups weren't the surprising part.

11
00:00:16,989 --> 00:00:19,084
What happened to my wrists, my brain

12
00:00:18,934 --> 00:00:20,458
and my belly was.

13
00:00:20,747 --> 00:00:21,776
Your belly?

14
00:00:21,626 --> 00:00:22,798
Now I'm listening.

15
00:00:23,637 --> 00:00:24,215
Day one.

16
00:00:24,484 --> 00:00:25,820
First, a test.

17
00:00:26,088 --> 00:00:28,634
One set, as many clean push-ups as

18
00:00:28,484 --> 00:00:29,139
I can.

19
00:00:29,429 --> 00:00:31,479
Clean means chest close to the floor,

20
00:00:31,549 --> 00:00:33,995
body straight like a plank, no sagging

21
00:00:33,846 --> 00:00:34,348
hips.

22
00:00:34,637 --> 00:00:35,370
Twenty-two.

23
00:00:35,637 --> 00:00:36,809
Then my arms quit.

24
00:00:37,099 --> 00:00:39,083
Twenty-two out of a hundred.

25
00:00:39,253 --> 00:00:39,687
So...

26
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:42,029
only seventy-eight to go.

27
00:00:42,319 --> 00:00:43,546
You don't do a hundred in one

28
00:00:43,396 --> 00:00:43,798
go.

29
00:00:44,066 --> 00:00:44,765
You split it.

30
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:47,193
Five sets of twenty, spread across the

31
00:00:47,044 --> 00:00:47,425
day.

32
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:51,491
Morning, lunch, afternoon, evening, and one angry

33
00:00:51,341 --> 00:00:52,238
set before bed.

34
00:00:52,527 --> 00:00:54,513
The angry set is my favourite.

35
00:00:54,802 --> 00:00:55,579
Total time?

36
00:00:55,846 --> 00:00:56,687
Eleven minutes.

37
00:00:56,956 --> 00:00:57,743
It felt easy.

38
00:00:58,011 --> 00:00:58,666
Too easy.

39
00:00:59,505 --> 00:01:00,128
Day two.

40
00:01:01,055 --> 00:01:02,842
I woke up, reached for my phone,

41
00:01:02,692 --> 00:01:04,666
and my chest said no.

42
00:01:04,956 --> 00:01:06,688
That's delayed muscle soreness.

43
00:01:06,956 --> 00:01:08,721
It peaks one to two days after

44
00:01:08,571 --> 00:01:10,139
something new, then it fades.

45
00:01:10,429 --> 00:01:12,117
So pain means growth, right?

46
00:01:12,407 --> 00:01:12,853
No.

47
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,645
Soreness means new.

48
00:01:14,736 --> 00:01:15,655
Not growth.

49
00:01:15,923 --> 00:01:17,491
You can grow without it, and you

50
00:01:17,341 --> 00:01:19,106
can be sore and grow nothing.

51
00:01:19,396 --> 00:01:21,117
Day three, I still did the hundred.

52
00:01:21,385 --> 00:01:22,754
But ten sets of ten.

53
00:01:23,022 --> 00:01:23,809
Slow.

54
00:01:24,066 --> 00:01:25,161
Form first.

55
00:01:25,451 --> 00:01:27,095
Ten sets of ten.

56
00:01:26,945 --> 00:01:29,436
That's just push-ups with extra steps.

57
00:01:29,725 --> 00:01:30,557
That's the point.

58
00:01:30,747 --> 00:01:33,721
Small sets, perfect reps, no grinding.

59
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,480
By day five, the soreness was gone.

60
00:01:36,747 --> 00:01:38,623
But my wrists started complaining.

61
00:01:38,912 --> 00:01:41,271
Seven hundred push-ups a week, every rep

62
00:01:41,121 --> 00:01:43,007
with the wrist bent back almost ninety

63
00:01:42,857 --> 00:01:43,502
degrees.

64
00:01:43,791 --> 00:01:44,985
The fix took ten seconds.

65
00:01:45,253 --> 00:01:47,227
Push-ups on my fists, or on two

66
00:01:47,077 --> 00:01:47,743
dumbbells.

67
00:01:48,011 --> 00:01:49,579
Wrist straight, pain gone.

68
00:01:49,868 --> 00:01:51,238
Fist push-ups.

69
00:01:51,264 --> 00:01:52,765
Very action movie.

70
00:01:53,055 --> 00:01:54,645
Second fix: elbows.

71
00:01:54,912 --> 00:01:56,447
If they flare out like a T,

72
00:01:56,516 --> 00:01:57,831
your shoulders take the hit.

73
00:01:58,099 --> 00:02:00,513
Keep them about forty-five degrees from your

74
00:02:00,451 --> 00:02:00,787
body.

75
00:02:01,077 --> 00:02:02,480
Day seven, I tested again.

76
00:02:02,747 --> 00:02:03,590
Twenty-seven.

77
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:05,677
Five more in one week.

78
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:07,007
Muscle already?

79
00:02:07,297 --> 00:02:07,952
Not yet.

80
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:09,875
That's my brain learning the move.

81
00:02:10,143 --> 00:02:11,458
The muscle part comes later.

82
00:02:13,121 --> 00:02:15,051
Week two felt like cheating.

83
00:02:15,319 --> 00:02:17,919
Same body, but the sets got easier

84
00:02:17,769 --> 00:02:18,425
every day.

85
00:02:18,714 --> 00:02:21,535
In the first weeks, most strength gains

86
00:02:21,385 --> 00:02:23,765
come from your nervous system, not new

87
00:02:23,615 --> 00:02:24,227
muscle.

88
00:02:24,516 --> 00:02:26,227
Your brain learns to switch on more

89
00:02:26,077 --> 00:02:28,623
muscle fibres, at the same time, and

90
00:02:28,473 --> 00:02:30,381
stops the muscles fighting each other.

91
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:33,007
So your muscles didn't grow.

92
00:02:33,242 --> 00:02:34,007
They just got...

93
00:02:34,231 --> 00:02:35,205
organised.

94
00:02:35,495 --> 00:02:36,150
Exactly.

95
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:38,227
Same team, better teamwork.

96
00:02:38,516 --> 00:02:40,469
Day fourteen: thirty-one.

97
00:02:40,758 --> 00:02:42,721
And then the real enemy showed up.

98
00:02:42,989 --> 00:02:43,952
Boredom.

99
00:02:44,242 --> 00:02:45,853
The push-ups were winning.

100
00:02:46,143 --> 00:02:48,106
So I stopped making it a workout.

101
00:02:48,352 --> 00:02:49,612
I made it a habit.

102
00:02:49,879 --> 00:02:52,315
Ten push-ups every time I made coffee.

103
00:02:52,582 --> 00:02:54,271
Ten every time I came back from

104
00:02:54,121 --> 00:02:54,820
the bathroom.

105
00:02:55,110 --> 00:02:57,480
By evening, the hundred was done and

106
00:02:57,330 --> 00:02:58,787
I never "worked out".

107
00:02:59,626 --> 00:03:00,875
Okay, week three.

108
00:03:01,648 --> 00:03:02,227
Abs?

109
00:03:02,396 --> 00:03:03,282
Huge chest?

110
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:04,128
Movie star?

111
00:03:04,418 --> 00:03:06,040
Chest and the back of my arms

112
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:07,205
looked a little fuller.

113
00:03:07,473 --> 00:03:09,381
Mostly a pump, and a little real

114
00:03:09,231 --> 00:03:09,798
growth.

115
00:03:10,088 --> 00:03:11,546
And my posture changed.

116
00:03:11,813 --> 00:03:14,018
A push-up is basically a moving plank.

117
00:03:14,286 --> 00:03:15,765
Your core works the whole time.

118
00:03:16,055 --> 00:03:16,985
And the belly?

119
00:03:17,275 --> 00:03:18,062
Same belly.

120
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:20,875
One hundred push-ups burn maybe thirty to

121
00:03:20,725 --> 00:03:21,842
fifty calories.

122
00:03:22,132 --> 00:03:23,381
That's one biscuit.

123
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:24,842
One biscuit?

124
00:03:24,813 --> 00:03:27,348
Three weeks of pain for one biscuit?

125
00:03:27,637 --> 00:03:29,018
Push-ups build strength.

126
00:03:29,286 --> 00:03:31,194
Fat loss comes from what you eat

127
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,414
and how much you walk.

128
00:03:32,681 --> 00:03:33,480
Different jobs.

129
00:03:33,769 --> 00:03:35,864
Day twenty-one: thirty-five.

130
00:03:36,703 --> 00:03:38,645
Week four, the hundred was easy.

131
00:03:38,912 --> 00:03:41,084
Four sets of twenty-five, done in ten

132
00:03:40,934 --> 00:03:41,524
minutes.

133
00:03:41,813 --> 00:03:42,831
And that's the problem.

134
00:03:43,099 --> 00:03:45,150
When something gets easy, the body stops

135
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:45,765
changing.

136
00:03:46,033 --> 00:03:47,304
It has no reason to.

137
00:03:47,593 --> 00:03:49,710
So the challenge stops being a challenge.

138
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,425
Right.

139
00:03:50,692 --> 00:03:52,765
Muscles grow when you keep asking for

140
00:03:52,615 --> 00:03:53,425
a little more.

141
00:03:53,714 --> 00:03:54,842
So I made them harder.

142
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:57,216
Three seconds down, one second up.

143
00:03:57,484 --> 00:03:59,106
Then feet on a chair.

144
00:03:59,396 --> 00:04:01,974
A study in 2017 found push-ups built

145
00:04:01,824 --> 00:04:03,568
chest muscle about as well as the

146
00:04:03,418 --> 00:04:05,359
bench press, as long as they kept

147
00:04:05,209 --> 00:04:06,007
getting harder.

148
00:04:06,297 --> 00:04:07,908
So the floor is a gym.

149
00:04:07,923 --> 00:04:08,524
Who knew?

150
00:04:09,363 --> 00:04:10,095
Day thirty.

151
00:04:10,363 --> 00:04:11,754
Same test as day one.

152
00:04:12,022 --> 00:04:13,853
One set, clean form.

153
00:04:14,143 --> 00:04:15,557
Drumroll please.

154
00:04:15,846 --> 00:04:16,676
Thirty-eight.

155
00:04:16,945 --> 00:04:19,611
From twenty-two to thirty-eight in thirty days.

156
00:04:19,901 --> 00:04:21,281
Here's the honest summary.

157
00:04:21,548 --> 00:04:22,919
Strength: way up.

158
00:04:23,187 --> 00:04:24,842
Endurance: way up.

159
00:04:25,110 --> 00:04:26,864
Chest and arms: a little bigger.

160
00:04:27,132 --> 00:04:28,491
Posture: better.

161
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,688
Belly fat: no change.

162
00:04:30,956 --> 00:04:32,743
And my wrists only survived because of

163
00:04:32,593 --> 00:04:33,238
the fix.

164
00:04:33,527 --> 00:04:34,808
So, would you do it again?

165
00:04:35,099 --> 00:04:35,721
Yes.

166
00:04:35,989 --> 00:04:37,292
But the smarter version.

167
00:04:38,132 --> 00:04:38,775
Rule one.

168
00:04:39,044 --> 00:04:40,666
Split the reps across the day.

169
00:04:40,934 --> 00:04:42,885
Never grind one ugly set.

170
00:04:43,176 --> 00:04:43,820
Rule two.

171
00:04:44,088 --> 00:04:45,556
Take one easy day a week.

172
00:04:45,824 --> 00:04:47,633
Fifty instead of a hundred.

173
00:04:47,901 --> 00:04:50,094
Joints recover slower than muscles.

174
00:04:50,385 --> 00:04:51,106
Rule three.

175
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:53,447
After two weeks, make it harder.

176
00:04:53,670 --> 00:04:55,655
Slower reps, or feet up.

177
00:04:55,945 --> 00:04:57,907
And if you can't do one push-up?

178
00:04:58,198 --> 00:04:59,941
Start on your knees, or with your

179
00:04:59,791 --> 00:05:01,370
hands on a wall or a table.

180
00:05:01,637 --> 00:05:03,424
Same muscles, less weight.

181
00:05:03,692 --> 00:05:05,952
A hundred wall push-ups still counts.

182
00:05:06,791 --> 00:05:09,007
Do the day one test right now.

183
00:05:09,275 --> 00:05:11,084
One set, clean form.

184
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:12,775
Write your number in the comments.

185
00:05:13,066 --> 00:05:14,919
Then come back in thirty days and

186
00:05:14,769 --> 00:05:15,698
write the new one.

187
00:05:15,989 --> 00:05:16,897
No lying.

188
00:05:16,857 --> 00:05:17,996
We will know.
